<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qara Iskander</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1438">1438</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Qara Iskandar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qara Iskander was ruler of the Qara Qoyunlu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> confederation from 1420, after the death of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a>. He held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> but was repeatedly defeated by the Timurid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-rukh">Shah Rukh</a>, who campaigned against him in 1421, 1429 and 1434–1435 and set up his brother Jahan Shah as a rival. Driven from his lands, he was killed in 1438 by his own son Shah Qubad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qara-iskander.jpg" alt="Qara Iskander" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1430 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iskandar_ibn_Qara_Yusuf_(contemporary_portrait,_painted_circa_1430).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
